<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The sources this repository restores from, and only these.

  The clear element is the whole point of the file. Without it NuGet adds whatever sources the
  machine has configured, and this repository uses central package management, which refuses to
  restore at all when there is more than one source and no package source mapping (NU1507). A
  developer who adds a private feed for unrelated work then cannot build this, and the error names
  neither the feed nor this repository.

  Worse than the error is the case where it succeeds. Two feeds mean a package could resolve from
  either, so a clone restores something different depending on what else the machine happens to
  trust. A library whose own build is not reproducible from a clean checkout has no business
  promising anything about its output.

  Behind a mirror or a proxy, change the value below rather than adding a second entry. A second
  entry brings NU1507 back.
-->
<configuration>
  <packageSources>
    <clear />
    <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" />
  </packageSources>
</configuration>
